{"id":"mahabharata-7-102","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":102,"title":"द्व्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 102 · Bhima goes to meet Satyaki","summary":{"en":"As Drona's army is churned by the Pandavas, Bhima, urged by Yudhishthira's anxiety, charges after Satyaki and Arjuna, and he strikes down the warriors in his way with a mighty roar.","kn":"ಪಾಂಡವರಿಂದ ದ್ರೋಣನ ಸೈನ್ಯ ಕಲಕಲ್ಪಡುತ್ತಿರಲು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನ ಆತಂಕದಿಂದ ಪ್ರೇರಿತ ಭೀಮ ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿ, ಅರ್ಜುನರ ಹಿಂದೆ ಧಾವಿಸಿ ದಾರಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಸಿಕ್ಕ ವೀರರನ್ನು ಗರ್ಜಿಸುತ್ತಾ ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"पाण्डवों द्वारा द्रोण की सेना मथी जाने पर युधिष्ठिर की चिन्ता से प्रेरित भीम सात्यकि और अर्जुन के पीछे दौड़ते हैं, और मार्ग के योद्धाओं को गर्जना के साथ मारते हैं।","te":"పాండవులచే ద్రోణుని సేన కలత చెందుతుండగా యుధిష్ఠిరుని ఆందోళనతో ప్రేరితుడై భీముడు సాత్యకి, అర్జునుల వెంట పరుగెత్తి దారిలోని వీరులను గర్జిస్తూ కూల్చుతాడు.","ta":"பாண்டவரால் த்ரோணரின் படை கலங்க, யுதிஷ்டிரரின் கவலையால் தூண்டப்பட்ட பீமன் சாத்யகி, அர்ஜுனனைத் தொடர்ந்து பாய்ந்து வழியிலுள்ள வீரரை முழங்கியபடி வீழ்த்துகிறான்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവർ ദ്രോണരുടെ സേനയെ ഇളക്കിമറിക്കുമ്പോൾ, യുധിഷ്ഠിരന്റെ ഉത്കണ്ഠയാൽ പ്രേരിതനായ ഭീമൻ സാത്യകിയെയും അർജുനനെയും തേടി പാഞ്ഞുപോകുന്നു; വഴിയിലുള്ള യോദ്ധാക്കളെ ഭയങ്കര ഗർജനത്തോടെ അദ്ദേഹം വെട്ടിവീഴ്ത്തുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.102; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"व्यूहेष्वालोड्यमानेषु पाण्डवानां ततस्ततः ।\nसुदूरमन्वयुः पार्थाः पाञ्चालाः सह सोमकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the Pandava formations were being churned here and there, the sons of Pritha and the Panchalas with the Somakas followed far into the battle."}},{"n":2,"text":"वर्तमाने तथा रौद्रे संग्रामे लोमहर्षणे ।\nप्रक्षये जगतस्तीव्रे युगान्त इव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"While that terrible, hair-raising battle went on, O Bharata, in the fierce destruction of the world as at an age's end,"}},{"n":3,"text":"द्रोणे युधि पराक्रान्ते नर्दमाने मुहुर्मुहुः ।\nपाञ्चालेषु च क्षीणेषु वध्यमानेषु पाण्डुषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"with Drona fighting valiantly and roaring again and again, and the Panchalas dwindling and the Pandavas being slaughtered,"}},{"n":4,"text":"नापश्यच्छरणं किंचिद्धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nचिन्तयामास राजेन्द्र कथमेतद्भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, king of dharma, saw no refuge anywhere. He thought, O king of kings, \"How will this end?\""}},{"n":5,"text":"तत्रावेक्ष्य दिशः सर्वाः सव्यसाचिदिदृक्षया ।\nयुधिष्ठिरो ददर्शाथ नैव पार्थं न माधवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Looking in every direction, wishing to see Arjuna, Yudhishthira saw neither Partha nor Madhava."}},{"n":6,"text":"सोऽपश्यन्नरशार्दूलं वानरर्षभलक्षणम् ।\nगाण्डीवस्य च निर्घोषमशृण्वन्व्यथितेन्द्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He did not see that tiger among men whose banner bears the sign of the monkey chief, and hearing no twang of the Gandiva, he was troubled in his senses."}},{"n":7,"text":"अपश्यन्सात्यकिं चापि वृष्णीनां प्रवरं रथम् ।\nचिन्तयाभिपरीताङ्गो धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nनाध्यगच्छत्तदा शान्तिं तावपश्यन्नरर्षभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw Satyaki too, best chariot of the Vrishnis, missing. Overcome with worry, Yudhishthira, king of dharma, found no peace, seeing neither of those two bulls among men."}},{"n":8,"text":"लोकोपक्रोशभीरुत्वाद्धर्मराजो महायशाः ।\nअचिन्तयन्महाबाहुः शैनेयस्य रथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The greatly renowned king of dharma, fearing the world's censure, mighty-armed, turned his thoughts to Satyaki's chariot."}},{"n":9,"text":"पदवीं प्रेषितश्चैव फल्गुनस्य मया रणे ।\nशैनेयः सात्यकिः सत्यो मित्राणामभयंकरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In the fight I sent Satyaki, Shini's descendant, the truthful one who gives his friends fearlessness, to follow Phalguna's path.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"तदिदं ह्येकमेवासीद्द्विधा जातं ममाद्य वै ।\nसात्यकिश्च हि मे ज्ञेयः पाण्डवश्च धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So what was one has today become two for me: I must keep track of Satyaki and of the Pandava Dhananjaya.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"सात्यकिं प्रेषयित्वा तु पाण्डवस्य पदानुगम् ।\nसात्वतस्यापि कं युद्धे प्रेषयिष्ये पदानुगम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having sent Satyaki to follow the Pandava's track, whom shall I send in battle to follow Satvata's track?\""}},{"n":12,"text":"करिष्यामि प्रयत्नेन भ्रातुरन्वेषणं यदि ।\nयुयुधानमनन्विष्य लोको मां गर्हयिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If I go to the trouble of searching for my brother, the world will blame me for not looking for Yuyudhana.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"भ्रातुरन्वेषणं कृत्वा धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nपरित्यजति वार्ष्णेयं सात्यकिं सत्यविक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"For the king of dharma, having searched for his brother, abandons the Vrishni Satyaki of true valor.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"लोकापवादभीरुत्वात्सोऽहं पार्थं वृकोदरम् ।\nपदवीं प्रेषयिष्यामि माधवस्य महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Out of fear of the world's reproach, I will therefore send the Pandava Vrikodara to follow the path of the great-souled Madhava's follower.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"यथैव च मम प्रीतिरर्जुने शत्रुसूदने ।\nतथैव वृष्णिवीरेऽपि सात्वते युद्धदुर्मदे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"As my affection is for Arjuna, slayer of foes, so it is for the Vrishni hero Satvata, who is wild in battle.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"अतिभारे नियुक्तश्च मया शैनेयनन्दनः ।\nस तु मित्रोपरोधेन गौरवाच्च महाबलः ।\nप्रविष्टो भारतीं सेनां मकरः सागरं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I put the son of Shini's grandson to a very heavy task. Out of regard for his friend and from respect, that mighty man entered the Bharata army like a sea monster into the ocean.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"असौ हि श्रूयते शब्दः शूराणामनिवर्तिनाम् ।\nमिथः संयुध्यमानानां वृष्णिवीरेण धीमता ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There is heard the sound of the heroes who never turn back, as they fight one another with the wise Vrishni hero.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"प्राप्तकालं सुबलवन्निश्चित्य बहुधा हि मे ।\nतत्रैव पाण्डवेयस्य भीमसेनस्य धन्विनः ।\nगमनं रोचते मह्यं यत्र यातौ महारथौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"After deciding in many ways that the time has come and is pressing, I think it best that the bowman Bhimasena, the Pandava, go to where the two great chariot-warriors have gone.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"न चाप्यसह्यं भीमस्य विद्यते भुवि किंचन ।\nशक्तो ह्येष रणे यत्तान्पृथिव्यां सर्वधन्विनः ।\nस्वबाहुबलमास्थाय प्रतिव्यूहितुमञ्जसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Nothing on earth is beyond Bhima's power. In battle he can, by his own arm's strength, readily face all the archers of the earth when they exert themselves.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"यस्य बाहुबलं सर्वे समाश्रित्य महात्मनः ।\nवनवासान्निवृत्ताः स्म न च युद्धेषु निर्जिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Relying on the arm-strength of that great-souled man, we all came back from the forest life and were not conquered in battles.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"इतो गते भीमसेने सात्वतं प्रति पाण्डवे ।\nसनाथौ भवितारौ हि युधि सात्वतफल्गुनौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When Bhimasena, the Pandava, goes from here after Satvata, the Satvata and Phalguna will have a protector in the fight.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"कामं त्वशोचनीयौ तौ रणे सात्वतफल्गुनौ ।\nरक्षितौ वासुदेवेन स्वयं चास्त्रविशारदौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Though those two, the Satvata and Phalguna, need not be mourned, since they are protected by Vasudeva himself and are expert in weapons,\""}},{"n":23,"text":"अवश्यं तु मया कार्यमात्मनः शोकनाशनम् ।\nतस्माद्भीमं नियोक्ष्यामि सात्वतस्य पदानुगम् ।\nततः प्रतिकृतं मन्ये विधानं सात्यकिं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I must certainly do what removes my own grief. So I will send Bhima to follow the Satvata. I think that would answer what is needed for Satyaki.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"एवं निश्चित्य मनसा धर्मपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nयन्तारमब्रवीद्राजन्भीमं प्रति नयस्व माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having so decided in his mind, Yudhishthira, son of Dharma, said to his charioteer, O king, \"Take me to Bhima.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"धर्मराजवचः श्रुत्वा सारथिर्हयकोविदः ।\nरथं हेमपरिष्कारं भीमान्तिकमुपानयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the king of dharma's words, the charioteer, skilled with horses, brought the gold-fitted chariot near Bhima."}},{"n":26,"text":"भीमसेनमनुप्राप्य प्राप्तकालमनुस्मरन् ।\nकश्मलं प्राविशद्राजा बहु तत्र समादिशन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Bhimasena and recalling that the time had come, the king fell into dejection, giving him many orders there."}},{"n":27,"text":"यः सदेवान्सगन्धर्वान्दैत्यांश्चैकरथोऽजयत् ।\nतस्य लक्ष्म न पश्यामि भीमसेनानुजस्य ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I cannot see any sign of your younger brother, who with a single chariot conquered the gods, gandharvas and daityas.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"ततोऽब्रवीद्धर्मराजं भीमसेनस्तथागतम् ।\nनैवाद्राक्षं न चाश्रौषं तव कश्मलमीदृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhimasena said to the king of dharma, who had come in that state, \"I have never seen nor heard of such dejection in you.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"पुरा हि दुःखदीर्णानां भवान्गतिरभूद्धि नः ।\nउत्तिष्ठोत्तिष्ठ राजेन्द्र शाधि किं करवाणि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In the past, when we were torn by sorrow, you were our refuge. Rise, rise, king of kings. Command me: what shall I do for you?\""}},{"n":30,"text":"न ह्यसाध्यमकार्यं वा विद्यते मम मानद ।\nआज्ञापय कुरुश्रेष्ठ मा च शोके मनः कृथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"For me, giver of honor, nothing is impossible or not to be done. Command, best of the Kurus, and do not set your mind on grief.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"तमब्रवीदश्रुपूर्णः कृष्णसर्प इव श्वसन् ।\nभीमसेनमिदं वाक्यं प्रम्लानवदनो नृपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With tears filling his eyes, sighing like a black snake and with a withered face, the king said this to Bhimasena."}},{"n":32,"text":"यथा शङ्खस्य निर्घोषः पाञ्चजन्यस्य श्रूयते ।\nप्रेरितो वासुदेवेन संरब्धेन यशस्विना ।\nनूनमद्य हतः शेते तव भ्राता धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The sound of the conch Panchajanya, blown by the furious, renowned Vasudeva, is heard as before; surely your brother Dhananjaya lies slain today.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"तस्मिन्विनिहते नूनं युध्यतेऽसौ जनार्दनः ।\nयस्य सत्त्ववतो वीर्यमुपजीवन्ति पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"With him slain, Janardana is surely fighting there, on whose strength and courage the Pandavas live.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"यं भयेष्वभिगच्छन्ति सहस्राक्षमिवामराः ।\nस शूरः सैन्धवप्रेप्सुरन्वयाद्भारतीं चमूम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The hero to whom they turn in fear as the immortals turn to the thousand-eyed Indra, wanting Saindhava, followed into the Bharata army.\""}},{"n":35,"text":"तस्य वै गमनं विद्मो भीम नावर्तनं पुनः ।\nश्यामो युवा गुडाकेशो दर्शनीयो महाभुजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"We know his going, Bhima, but not his return, that dark young Gudakesha, handsome, long-armed,\""}},{"n":36,"text":"व्यूढोरस्को महास्कन्धो मत्तद्विरदविक्रमः ।\nचकोरनेत्रस्ताम्राक्षो द्विषतामघवर्धनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"broad-chested, great-shouldered, who walks like a rutting elephant, with eyes like a chakora's, copper-red, increaser of his enemies' woe.\""}},{"n":37,"text":"तदिदं मम भद्रं ते शोकस्थानमरिंदम ।\nअर्जुनार्थं महाबाहो सात्वतस्य च कारणात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So this, good fortune to you, is the cause of my grief, tamer of foes, mighty-armed, for Arjuna's sake and for the Satvata's.\""}},{"n":38,"text":"वर्धते हविषेवाग्निरिध्यमानः पुनः पुनः ।\nतस्य लक्ष्म न पश्यामि तेन विन्दामि कश्मलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He grows like a fire fed again and again with oblations. I cannot see his sign, and so I fall into dejection.\""}},{"n":39,"text":"तं विद्धि पुरुषव्याघ्रं सात्वतं च महारथम् ।\nस तं महारथं पश्चादनुयातस्तवानुजम् ।\nतमपश्यन्महाबाहुमहं विन्दामि कश्मलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Know that tiger among men and the great chariot-warrior Satvata, who followed your younger brother, that great chariot-warrior. Not seeing the mighty-armed one, I fall into dejection.\""}},{"n":40,"text":"तस्मात्कृष्णो रणे नूनं युध्यते युद्धकोविदः ।\nयस्य वीर्यवतो वीर्यमुपजीवन्ति पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So surely Krishna, expert in war, is fighting in the battle, on whose powerful strength the Pandavas live.\""}},{"n":41,"text":"स तत्र गच्छ कौन्तेय यत्र यातो धनंजयः ।\nसात्यकिश्च महावीर्यः कर्तव्यं यदि मन्यसे ।\nवचनं मम धर्मज्ञ ज्येष्ठो भ्राता भवामि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Go, son of Kunti, there where Dhananjaya has gone, and the very mighty Satyaki too, if you think my word should be done. Knower of dharma, I am your elder brother.\""}},{"n":42,"text":"न तेऽर्जुनस्तथा ज्ञेयो ज्ञातव्यः सात्यकिर्यथा ।\nचिकीर्षुर्मत्प्रियं पार्थ प्रयातः सव्यसाचिनः ।\nपदवीं दुर्गमां घोरामगम्यामकृतात्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You must not look on Arjuna as you must look on Satyaki. Wishing to do what pleases me, he went on the left-handed archer's path, fearful, hard to travel, and unreachable for those with unformed selves.\""}},{"text":"भीमसेन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena said:"}},{"n":43,"text":"ब्रह्मेशानेन्द्रवरुणानवहद्यः पुरा रथः ।\nतमास्थाय गतौ कृष्णौ न तयोर्विद्यते भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The chariot that once carried Brahma, Ishana, Indra and Varuna, mounting it the two Krishnas have gone. There is no fear for them.\""}},{"n":44,"text":"आज्ञां तु शिरसा बिभ्रदेष गच्छामि मा शुचः ।\nसमेत्य तान्नरव्याघ्रांस्तव दास्यामि संविदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"But bearing your command on my head, I go; do not grieve. Having met those two tigers among men, I will bring you word.\""}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":45,"text":"एतावदुक्त्वा प्रययौ परिदाय युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नाय बलवान्सुहृद्भ्यश्च पुनः पुनः ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नं चेदमाह भीमसेनो महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this much, the strong Bhima left, entrusting Yudhishthira again and again to Dhrishtadyumna and his friends. The mighty Bhimasena said this to Dhrishtadyumna."}},{"n":46,"text":"विदितं ते महाबाहो यथा द्रोणो महारथः ।\nग्रहणे धर्मराजस्य सर्वोपायेन वर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You know, mighty-armed one, how the great chariot-warrior Drona is working by every means to capture the king of dharma.\""}},{"n":47,"text":"न च मे गमने कृत्यं तादृक्पार्षत विद्यते ।\nयादृशं रक्षणे राज्ञः कार्यमात्ययिकं हि नः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Such a task as going does not weigh on me as much as guarding the king, which is for us the urgent duty.\""}},{"n":48,"text":"एवमुक्तोऽस्मि पार्थेन प्रतिवक्तुं स्म नोत्सहे ।\nप्रयास्ये तत्र यत्रासौ मुमूर्षुः सैन्धवः स्थितः ।\nधर्मराजस्य वचने स्थातव्यमविशङ्कया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"But Partha has told me so, and I do not dare answer back. I shall go where Saindhava, who seeks death, stands. The word of the king of dharma must be kept without doubt.\""}},{"n":49,"text":"सोऽद्य यत्तो रणे पार्थं परिरक्ष युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nएतद्धि सर्वकार्याणां परमं कृत्यमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So today, be careful in the fight and protect Yudhishthira, son of Pritha. That is the highest of all tasks in battle.\""}},{"n":50,"text":"तमब्रवीन्महाराज धृष्टद्युम्नो वृकोदरम् ।\nईप्सितेन महाबाहो गच्छ पार्थाविचारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna said to Vrikodara, great king, \"Go, mighty-armed one, as you wish, without hesitation.\""}},{"n":51,"text":"नाहत्वा समरे द्रोणो धृष्टद्युम्नं कथंचन ।\nनिग्रहं धर्मराजस्य प्रकरिष्यति संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Drona will never, in any way, take the king of dharma captive in battle without first killing me.\""}},{"n":52,"text":"ततो निक्षिप्य राजानं धृष्टद्युम्नाय पाण्डवः ।\nअभिवाद्य गुरुं ज्येष्ठं प्रययौ यत्र फल्गुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Pandava, entrusting the king to Dhrishtadyumna and saluting his eldest brother, went where Phalguna was."}},{"n":53,"text":"परिष्वक्तस्तु कौन्तेयो धर्मराजेन भारत ।\nआघ्रातश्च तथा मूर्ध्नि श्रावितश्चाशिषः शुभाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Kunti, O Bharata, was embraced by the king of dharma, who smelled his head and spoke auspicious blessings."}},{"n":54,"text":"भीमसेनो महाबाहुः कवची शुभकुण्डली ।\nसाङ्गदः सतनुत्राणः सशरी रथिनां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mighty-armed Bhimasena, best of chariot-fighters, wore armor, bright earrings, armlets and body-guard, and carried his arrows."}},{"n":55,"text":"तस्य कार्ष्णायसं वर्म हेमचित्रं महर्द्धिमत् ।\nविबभौ पर्वतश्लिष्टः सविद्युदिव तोयदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His black-iron armor, adorned with gold and very splendid, shone like a cloud with lightning clinging to a mountain."}},{"n":56,"text":"पीतरक्तासितसितैर्वासोभिश्च सुवेष्टितः ।\nकण्ठत्राणेन च बभौ सेन्द्रायुध इवाम्बुदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wrapped in garments of yellow, red, black and white, with a neck-guard, he shone like a cloud with Indra's bow."}},{"n":57,"text":"प्रयाते भीमसेने तु तव सैन्यं युयुत्सया ।\nपाञ्चजन्यरवो घोरः पुनरासीद्विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Bhimasena had gone, a terrible sound of Panchajanya was heard again, lord of the people, among your army eager to fight."}},{"n":58,"text":"तं श्रुत्वा निनदं घोरं त्रैलोक्यत्रासनं महत् ।\nपुनर्भीमं महाबाहुर्धर्मपुत्रोऽभ्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that dreadful, great roar that terrified the three worlds, the mighty-armed son of Dharma spoke to Bhima again."}},{"n":59,"text":"एष वृष्णिप्रवीरेण ध्मातः सलिलजो भृशम् ।\nपृथिवीं चान्तरिक्षं च विनादयति शङ्खराट् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This is the conch, born of water, blown hard by the great Vrishni hero, filling earth and sky with its sound.\""}},{"n":60,"text":"नूनं व्यसनमापन्ने सुमहत्सव्यसाचिनि ।\nकुरुभिर्युध्यते सार्धं सर्वैश्चक्रगदाधरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely, with Arjuna fallen into great trouble, the bearer of the discus and mace is fighting all the Kurus.\""}},{"n":61,"text":"नूनमार्या महत्कुन्ती पापमद्य निदर्शनम् ।\nद्रौपदी च सुभद्रा च पश्यन्ति सह बन्धुभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely noble Kunti, Draupadi and Subhadra, with their kin, are seeing a great evil omen today.\""}},{"n":62,"text":"स भीमस्त्वरया युक्तो याहि यत्र धनंजयः ।\nमुह्यन्तीव हि मे सर्वा धनंजयदिदृक्षया ।\nदिशः सप्रदिशः पार्थ सात्वतस्य च कारणात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So, Bhima, go quickly to where Dhananjaya is. All the directions and corners seem to whirl for me from my longing to see Dhananjaya, Partha, and for the Satvata's sake.\""}},{"n":63,"text":"गच्छ गच्छेति च पुनर्भीमसेनमभाषत ।\nभृशं स प्रहितो भ्रात्रा भ्राता भ्रातुः प्रियंकरः ।\nआहत्य दुन्दुभिं भीमः शङ्खं प्रध्माय चासकृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He said again to Bhimasena, \"Go, go.\" Urged strongly by his brother, Bhima, doing a brother's wish, struck his drum, blew his conch again and again,"}},{"n":64,"text":"विनद्य सिंहनादं च ज्यां विकर्षन्पुनः पुनः ।\nदर्शयन्घोरमात्मानममित्रान्सहसाभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"roared a lion's roar, and drew his bowstring repeatedly, showing his terrible self, and suddenly charged the enemies."}},{"n":65,"text":"तमूहुर्जवना दान्ता विकुर्वाणा हयोत्तमाः ।\nविशोकेनाभिसंयत्ता मनोमारुतरंहसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His swift, well-trained, fine horses, driven by Vishoka, bore him, quick as mind and wind."}},{"n":66,"text":"आरुजन्विरुजन्पार्थो ज्यां विकर्षंश्च पाणिना ।\nसोऽवकर्षन्विकर्षंश्च सेनाग्रं समलोडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Breaking and splitting, Partha pulled the bowstring with his hand, and drawing and dragging, he churned the front of their army."}},{"n":67,"text":"तं प्रयान्तं महाबाहुं पाञ्चालाः सहसोमकाः ।\nपृष्ठतोऽनुययुः शूरा मघवन्तमिवामराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that mighty-armed one went, the Panchalas with the Somakas, brave men, followed behind him as the immortals follow Indra."}},{"n":68,"text":"तं ससेना महाराज सोदर्याः पर्यवारयन् ।\nदुःशलश्चित्रसेनश्च कुण्डभेदी विविंशतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, your brothers surrounded him with their troops: Duhshala, Chitrasena, Kundabhedin, Vivimshati,"}},{"n":69,"text":"दुर्मुखो दुःसहश्चैव विकर्णश्च शलस्तथा ।\nविन्दानुविन्दौ सुमुखो दीर्घबाहुः सुदर्शनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Durmukha, Duhsaha, Vikarna, Shala, Vinda and Anuvinda, Sumukha, Dirghabahu, Sudarshana,"}},{"n":70,"text":"वृन्दारकः सुहस्तश्च सुषेणो दीर्घलोचनः ।\nअभयो रौद्रकर्मा च सुवर्मा दुर्विमोचनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vrindaraka, Suhasta, Sushena, Dirghalochana, Abhaya, Raudrakarman, Suvarman, and Durvimochana."}},{"n":71,"text":"विविधै रथिनां श्रेष्ठाः सह सैन्यैः सहानुगैः ।\nसंयत्ताः समरे शूरा भीमसेनमुपाद्रवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those best of chariot-fighters, brave men, with various troops and followers, rushed against Bhimasena in the battle."}},{"n":72,"text":"तान्समीक्ष्य तु कौन्तेयो भीमसेनः पराक्रमी ।\nअभ्यवर्तत वेगेन सिंहः क्षुद्रमृगानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them, the valiant Bhimasena, son of Kunti, turned on them at speed, like a lion at small deer."}},{"n":73,"text":"ते महास्त्राणि दिव्यानि तत्र वीरा अदर्शयन् ।\nवारयन्तः शरैर्भीमं मेघाः सूर्यमिवोदितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those heroes displayed there great divine weapons, covering Bhima with arrows as clouds cover the risen sun."}},{"n":74,"text":"स तानतीत्य वेगेन द्रोणानीकमुपाद्रवत् ।\nअग्रतश्च गजानीकं शरवर्षैरवाकिरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He passed them with speed and attacked Drona's division, and first scattered the elephant division with showers of arrows."}},{"n":75,"text":"सोऽचिरेणैव कालेन तद्गजानीकमाशुगैः ।\nदिशः सर्वाः समभ्यस्य व्यधमत्पवनात्मजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In no time the son of the Wind, practicing in every direction, shattered that elephant force with his arrows."}},{"n":76,"text":"त्रासिताः शरभस्येव गर्जितेन वने मृगाः ।\nप्राद्रवन्द्विरदाः सर्वे नदन्तो भैरवान्रवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Terrified, as forest beasts are by a sharabha's roar, all the elephants fled, trumpeting dreadful cries."}},{"n":77,"text":"पुनश्चातीत्य वेगेन द्रोणानीकमुपाद्रवत् ।\nतमवारयदाचार्यो वेलेवोद्वृत्तमर्णवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Again he passed them with speed and attacked Drona's division. The teacher checked him as the shore checks a surging sea."}},{"n":78,"text":"ललाटेऽताडयच्चैनं नाराचेन स्मयन्निव ।\nऊर्ध्वरश्मिरिवादित्यो विबभौ तत्र पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He struck him on the forehead with a nitaracha arrow, smiling as it were, and the Pandava shone there like the sun with upward rays."}},{"n":79,"text":"स मन्यमानस्त्वाचार्यो ममायं फल्गुनो यथा ।\nभीमः करिष्यते पूजामित्युवाच वृकोदरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking, \"This one is like Phalguna to me; Bhima will do me honor,\" he said to Vrikodara,"}},{"n":80,"text":"भीमसेन न ते शक्यं प्रवेष्टुमरिवाहिनीम् ।\nमामनिर्जित्य समरे शत्रुमध्ये महाबल ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Bhimasena, you cannot enter the enemy host without defeating me in battle, in the midst of the enemy, mighty one.\""}},{"n":81,"text":"यदि ते सोऽनुजः कृष्णः प्रविष्टोऽनुमते मम ।\nअनीकं न तु शक्यं भोः प्रवेष्टुमिह वै त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If your younger brother Krishna entered with my leave, you for your part cannot enter this division.\""}},{"n":82,"text":"अथ भीमस्तु तच्छ्रुत्वा गुरोर्वाक्यमपेतभीः ।\nक्रुद्धः प्रोवाच वै द्रोणं रक्तताम्रेक्षणः श्वसन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his teacher's words, Bhima, free of fear, angry, with eyes red as copper, sighing, said to Drona,"}},{"n":83,"text":"तवार्जुनो नानुमते ब्रह्मबन्धो रणाजिरम् ।\nप्रविष्टः स हि दुर्धर्षः शक्रस्यापि विशेद्बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Brahmin by name only, Arjuna did not enter the battlefield by your leave. That invincible one could enter even Shakra's force.\""}},{"n":84,"text":"येन वै परमां पूजां कुर्वता मानितो ह्यसि ।\nनार्जुनोऽहं घृणी द्रोण भीमसेनोऽस्मि ते रिपुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He, honoring you with the highest respect, showed you honor. I am not Arjuna, Drona, not tender: I am Bhimasena, your enemy.\""}},{"n":85,"text":"पिता नस्त्वं गुरुर्बन्धुस्तथा पुत्रा हि ते वयम् ।\nइति मन्यामहे सर्वे भवन्तं प्रणताः स्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You are our father, teacher and kinsman, and we are your sons; so we all think, standing bowed before you.\""}},{"n":86,"text":"अद्य तद्विपरीतं ते वदतोऽस्मासु दृश्यते ।\nयदि शत्रुं त्वमात्मानं मन्यसे तत्तथास्त्विह ।\nएष ते सदृशं शत्रोः कर्म भीमः करोम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today we see you speaking the opposite of that to us. If you regard yourself as an enemy, so be it. I, Bhima, do the deed fit for an enemy.\""}},{"n":87,"text":"अथोद्भ्राम्य गदां भीमः कालदण्डमिवान्तकः ।\nद्रोणायावसृजद्राजन्स रथादवपुप्लुवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhima whirled his mace, like Death with the staff of Time, and hurled it at Drona, O king, and leaped from his chariot."}},{"n":88,"text":"साश्वसूतध्वजं यानं द्रोणस्यापोथयत्तदा ।\nप्रामृद्नाच्च बहून्योधान्वायुर्वृक्षानिवौजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he smashed Drona's vehicle with its horses, charioteer and banner, and ground down many warriors with force as the wind does trees."}},{"n":89,"text":"तं पुनः परिवव्रुस्ते तव पुत्रा रथोत्तमम् ।\nअन्यं च रथमास्थाय द्रोणः प्रहरतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your sons again surrounded him, that best of chariot-fighters, and Drona, best of fighters, mounted another chariot."}},{"n":90,"text":"ततः क्रुद्धो महाराज भीमसेनः पराक्रमी ।\nअग्रतः स्यन्दनानीकं शरवर्षैरवाकिरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the valiant Bhimasena, enraged, great king, covered the front chariot division with showers of arrows."}},{"n":91,"text":"ते वध्यमानाः समरे तव पुत्रा महारथाः ।\nभीमं भीमबलं युद्धेऽयोधयंस्तु जयैषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Slaughtered in the battle, your sons, the great chariot-warriors, eager for victory, fought Bhima of terrible strength."}},{"n":92,"text":"ततो दुःशासनः क्रुद्धो रथशक्तिं समाक्षिपत् ।\nसर्वपारशवीं तीक्ष्णां जिघांसुः पाण्डुनन्दनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the angry Duhshasana hurled a chariot-javelin, sharp and made wholly of iron, wanting to kill the Pandava."}},{"n":93,"text":"आपतन्तीं महाशक्तिं तव पुत्रप्रचोदिताम् ।\nद्विधा चिच्छेद तां भीमस्तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima cut in two that great javelin flying at him, sent by your son, and it was marvelous."}},{"n":94,"text":"अथान्यैर्निशितैर्बाणैः संक्रुद्धः कुण्डभेदिनम् ।\nसुषेणं दीर्घनेत्रं च त्रिभिस्त्रीनवधीद्बली ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, angry, the strong one killed with other sharp arrows Kundabhedin, Sushena and Dirghanetra, three with three."}},{"n":95,"text":"ततो वृन्दारकं वीरं कुरूणां कीर्तिवर्धनम् ।\nपुत्राणां तव वीराणां युध्यतामवधीत्पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he killed the hero Vrindaraka, increaser of the Kurus' fame, among your heroic sons who were fighting."}},{"n":96,"text":"अभयं रौद्रकर्माणं दुर्विमोचनमेव च ।\nत्रिभिस्त्रीनवधीद्भीमः पुनरेव सुतांस्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima then killed Abhaya, Raudrakarman and Durvimochana, three of your sons, with three arrows."}},{"n":97,"text":"वध्यमाना महाराज पुत्रास्तव बलीयसा ।\nभीमं प्रहरतां श्रेष्ठं समन्तात्पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As your sons were being slaughtered by the stronger man, great king, the best of fighters surrounded Bhima on all sides."}},{"n":98,"text":"विन्दानुविन्दौ सहितौ सुवर्माणं च ते सुतम् ।\nप्रहसन्निव कौन्तेयः शरैर्निन्ये यमक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Laughing as it were, the son of Kunti sent Vinda and Anuvinda together, and your son Suvarman, to Yama's abode with arrows."}},{"n":99,"text":"ततः सुदर्शनं वीरं पुत्रं ते भरतर्षभ ।\nविव्याध समरे तूर्णं स पपात ममार च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O best of Bharatas, he quickly pierced your son, the hero Sudarshana, in battle; he fell and died."}},{"n":100,"text":"सोऽचिरेणैव कालेन तद्रथानीकमाशुगैः ।\nदिशः सर्वाः समभ्यस्य व्यधमत्पाण्डुनन्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In no time the son of Pandu, practicing in every direction, shattered that chariot division with his arrows."}},{"n":101,"text":"ततो वै रथघोषेण गर्जितेन मृगा इव ।\nवध्यमानाश्च समरे पुत्रास्तव विशां पते ।\nप्राद्रवन्सरथाः सर्वे भीमसेनभयार्दिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your sons, lord of the people, slaughtered in the battle, fled with their chariots, like beasts at a roar, tormented by fear of Bhimasena."}},{"n":102,"text":"अनुयाय तु कौन्तेयः पुत्राणां ते महद्बलम् ।\nविव्याध समरे राजन्कौरवेयान्समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Kunti pursued the great force of your sons, O king, and pierced the Kauravas on every side in the battle."}},{"n":103,"text":"वध्यमाना महाराज भीमसेनेन तावकाः ।\nत्यक्त्वा भीमं रणे यान्ति चोदयन्तो हयोत्तमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Slaughtered by Bhimasena, O great king, your men left Bhima and fled, driving their best horses."}},{"n":104,"text":"तांस्तु निर्जित्य समरे भीमसेनो महाबलः ।\nसिंहनादरवं चक्रे बाहुशब्दं च पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having defeated them in the battle, the mighty Pandava Bhimasena gave a lion's roar and a slap on his arms."}},{"n":105,"text":"तलशब्दं च सुमहत्कृत्वा भीमो महाबलः ।\nव्यतीत्य रथिनश्चापि द्रोणानीकमुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Making a great clap of his palms, mighty Bhima passed the chariot-warriors and attacked Drona's division."}}]}]}